---
profile: basic

exclude_paths:
  - .ansible/
  - collections/

skip_list:
  # Wants every variable in the role prefixed `config_`. That convention earns
  # its keep when roles are shared and their variables can collide; here there
  # is one role, the names are already domain-prefixed (crowdsec_*, docker_*,
  # fail2ban_*), and renaming ~50 variables would only add noise. ansible_port
  # is flagged by the same rule and cannot be renamed at all - it is Ansible's.
  - var-naming[no-role-prefix]

  # "Tasks that run when changed should likely be handlers." Not here: the four
  # matches are the mid-play SSH port switch and the sysctl apply, which must
  # run inline. Handlers fire at the end of the play, by which point sshd has
  # already moved and the connection would be dead.
  - no-handler
